  "blurb": "A newly completed villa high in the hills above Chaweng, laid out over three levels around an infinity-edge pool and wide, uninterrupted sea views. Four king-bed en-suite bedrooms, a top-floor master with a freestanding bath facing the ocean, and an air-conditioned home office. Freehold on a Chanote title, turnkey, and about four kilometres from Chaweng beach.",
  "detail": "Completed in 2025 on a private hillside plot above Chaweng, this villa is arranged across three levels so that the sea opens up from almost every room. The architecture is calm and contemporary — a crisp geometric façade softened by planting, white render offset by warm timber, and full-height glass that brings the light and the view deep into the house.\n\nThe ground floor is given over to open-plan living and dining, with a long timber table beneath sculptural pendants and a fully fitted kitchen built around an island, with oven and electric hob. Glass doors slide back onto the main terrace, where an infinity-edge pool runs out toward the horizon, alongside an outdoor rain shower and space for sunloungers and dining in the open air.\n\nAll four bedrooms take king-size beds, are en-suite with ducted air conditioning, and look out to sea. The master occupies the top floor on its own, with a walk-in dressing room and a freestanding bathtub positioned to face the treetops and the ocean. A further bedroom sits on the lower level for extra privacy — well suited to guests or older children — and a separate air-conditioned office makes the villa an easy base for working from home.\n\nThe approach is a steep hillside road best taken in a 4x4, which is part of what keeps the setting so private. Once there, Chaweng's beach, restaurants, international schools and supermarkets are around four kilometres away, and the airport about seven. Sold freehold on a Chanote title with 695 m² of building on an 887 m² plot, the villa is turnkey and suits a full-time home, a seasonal retreat or a rental investment.",
